# A browser that produces assets

Chromium supplies SVG layout and PDF vector printing; it does not typeset the
book. The worker loads the bundled Mermaid distribution through a connect-only
Puppeteer adapter, excluding browser management and download code. Each diagram
gets a new browser context, preventing one diagram's DOM and Mermaid counters
from affecting another. The controller owns the deadline, process group and temporary directory.


## Complete offline renderer graph

Mermaid distributes renderer definitions as lazy ESM chunks. Bundling the complete
ESM graph into one IIFE preserves their deferred initialization without making
network requests when a family is first used. ZenUML needs a separately registered
plugin; tidy-tree supplies an optional layout, not a new diagram family. Their
pinned packages are the same integrations offered by the Mermaid CLI. The plugin's
prebundled ESM distribution avoids importing its Node-facing rendering helpers.


The pinned ZenUML definition injects CSS containing a neon-theme font face whose
source is `/fonts/MS%20Sans%20Serif.ttf`. Forcing a sans-serif family does not remove
that downloadable face from the browser's font set. Before any diagram renders,
we remove only that exact rule from style elements introduced by the trusted
plugin loader. This is not a sanitizer for author CSS or arbitrary resources:
other rules remain unchanged, and a changed plugin rule still fails closed under
CSP and request interception. No font request or recorded violation is excused.

No diagram-type allowlist stands in front of Mermaid's detector. Unknown syntax
or unregistered third-party renderers fail explicitly. Remote icon registries,
external images, executable callbacks and author configuration remain disabled,
regardless of the family requesting them. A new renderer does not gain new browser
permissions merely by being registered.

## Local, fixed configuration

Only catalogue colors, the bounded publication font size, and fixed security
settings enter initialization. Source text cannot supply scripts, styles, callbacks,
directives or configuration. Stable IDs depend on source, theme, and size, not
processing order or wall-clock time. Classic
shapes and disabled filters avoid Chromium's rasterization of decorative shadows;
the selected palette still controls colors.

```js : <<Mermaid worker imports>>=
import * as fs from 'node:fs/promises';
import * as path from 'node:path';
import { createHash } from 'node:crypto';
import mermaidPackage from 'mermaid/package.json' with { type: 'json' };
import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';
import { spawn } from 'node:child_process';
import { getTheme, mermaidTheme } from './themes';
import { publicationFontSizeBounds } from './publication-settings';
import { diagramLimits, validateDiagram } from './publication-mermaid';

const hash = value => createHash('sha256').update(value).digest('hex');
export function configuration(theme, fontSize, seed) {
    const palette = mermaidTheme(getTheme(theme));
    return { ...palette, themeVariables: { ...palette.themeVariables, fontSize: `${fontSize}px` },
        startOnLoad: false,
        securityLevel: 'strict', look: 'classic', suppressErrorRendering: true, maxTextSize: 50000,
        maxEdges: 500, htmlLabels: false, flowchart: { htmlLabels: false },
        fontFamily: 'sans-serif', deterministicIds: true, deterministicIDSeed: seed,
        secure: ['secure', 'securityLevel', 'startOnLoad', 'suppressErrorRendering',
            'maxTextSize', 'maxEdges', 'theme', 'themeVariables', 'fontFamily',
            'htmlLabels', 'flowchart', 'look', 'deterministicIds', 'deterministicIDSeed'] };
}
```

A reserved origin is fulfilled once from an in-memory bootstrap document; no
DNS request or server is involved. This gives plugins an isolated storage origin
instead of the inaccessible storage of about:blank. The bundle is injected as
trusted code. CSP denies connections, files, images, fonts, frames and forms;
interception aborts every request other than that one bootstrap. Attempted
resources or navigation fail the diagram instead of producing an incomplete asset.

```js : <<Mermaid page isolation>>=
export async function isolatePage(page) {
    const violations = [];
    const origin = 'https://literate.invalid/';
    let bootstrap = true;
    page.setDefaultTimeout(15000);
    await page.setRequestInterception(true);
    <<Mermaid bootstrap interception>>
    page.on('framenavigated', frame => {
        if (frame.url() !== origin) { violations.push('navigation'); }
    });
    page.on('popup', popup => { violations.push('popup'); void popup.close().catch(() => {}); });
    await page.setBypassServiceWorker(true);
    await page.goto(origin, { waitUntil: 'load' });
    <<Mermaid CSP observation>>
    return violations;
}
```

The bootstrap response is fixed renderer code, never project HTML. Its CSP sandbox
allows scripts and same-origin storage, but not popups, forms or top navigation.
Every context has fresh storage. Neither plugin initialization nor diagram content
can use the bootstrap URL to request another document.

```js : <<Mermaid bootstrap interception>>=
page.on('request', request => {
    if (bootstrap && request.url() === origin && request.isNavigationRequest()
        && request.frame() === page.mainFrame()) {
        bootstrap = false;
        void request.respond({ status: 200, contentType: 'text/html', headers: {
            'Content-Security-Policy': "default-src 'none'; script-src 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; "
                + "connect-src 'none'; img-src 'none'; font-src 'none'; frame-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; "
                + "base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; sandbox allow-scripts allow-same-origin"
        }, body: '<!doctype html><style>html,body{margin:0;padding:0}svg{display:block}'
                    + '*,*::before,*::after{font-family:sans-serif!important}</style><body></body>'
        }).catch(error => violations.push(String(error)));
    } else {
        violations.push('resource request');
        void request.abort('blockedbyclient').catch(() => {});
    }
});
```

CSP can stop a fetch before it reaches request interception. The page records
those violations too. Code injected through the protocol is controlled by this
worker; there are no source-derived JavaScript strings or event bindings.

```js : <<Mermaid CSP observation>>=
await page.evaluate(() => {
    globalThis.publicationViolations = [];
    document.addEventListener('securitypolicyviolation', event => {
        globalThis.publicationViolations.push(event.violatedDirective + ': ' + event.blockedURI.slice(0, 200));
    });
});
```

## Validate the produced vector

Strict Mermaid rendering is not the only boundary. Reject active SVG elements,
external references and event handlers. Passive XHTML labels inside foreignObject
are permitted because some renderers require them even with htmlLabels disabled;
active HTML and all external resources remain forbidden. Local fragment references remain available
for markers and glyphs. CSS URLs must also refer to local fragments. These checks
run before printing or handing the SVG to the parent.

```js : <<Mermaid SVG geometry>>=
export function measureSvg() {
    const svg = document.querySelector('body > svg');
    if (!svg) { throw new Error('Mermaid returned no root SVG'); }
    if (svg.querySelector('script,image,img,a,iframe,object,embed,video,audio,animate,animateMotion,animateTransform,set,form,input,button')) {
        throw new Error('Mermaid SVG contains unsupported active or external content');
    }
    const checkCss = value => {
        if (/@import/i.test(value)) { throw new Error('External SVG CSS is disabled'); }
        for (const match of value.matchAll(/url\(([^)]*)\)/gi)) {
            if (!match[1].trim().replace(/^["']|["']$/g, '').startsWith('#')) {
                throw new Error('External SVG CSS resource is disabled');
            }
        }
    };
    <<Mermaid SVG attribute policy>>
    <<Mermaid SVG bounds>>
}
```

Presentation attributes are checked alongside style elements: an external paint
server must not bypass the style policy. The SVG is serialized only after its
geometry is fixed. No callback returned by Mermaid is installed.

```js : <<Mermaid SVG attribute policy>>=
for (const element of [svg, ...svg.querySelectorAll('*')]) {
    if (element.namespaceURI === 'http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml'
        && !['div', 'span', 'p', 'br', 'b', 'strong', 'i', 'em', 'small', 'code', 'pre',
            'table', 'thead', 'tbody', 'tr', 'td', 'th', 'ul', 'ol', 'li'].includes(element.localName)) {
        throw new Error('Unsupported active HTML in Mermaid label');
    }
    for (const attribute of element.attributes) {
        if (/^on/i.test(attribute.name) || (/href$/i.test(attribute.name) && !attribute.value.startsWith('#'))) {
            throw new Error('Mermaid SVG interaction or external reference is disabled');
        }
        checkCss(attribute.value);
    }
    if (element.localName === 'style') { checkCss(element.textContent); }
}
const fixed = document.createElementNS('http://www.w3.org/2000/svg', 'style');
fixed.textContent = '*,*::before,*::after{animation:none!important;transition:none!important;filter:none!important;font-family:sans-serif!important}';
svg.prepend(fixed);
```

Use the union of the declared view box and measured contents, plus an eight-pixel
safety border for strokes. Both dimensions and area are capped before printing.
The PDF paper matches this diagram rectangle, not the requested book paper.
The later LaTeX inclusion preserves its aspect ratio at the available body size.

```js : <<Mermaid SVG bounds>>=
const box = svg.getBBox(), view = svg.viewBox.baseVal;
const x = Math.min(box.x, view.x) - 8, y = Math.min(box.y, view.y) - 8;
const width = Math.ceil(Math.max(box.x + box.width, view.x + view.width) - x + 8);
const height = Math.ceil(Math.max(box.y + box.height, view.y + view.height) - y + 8);
if (![x, y, width, height].every(Number.isFinite) || width < 1 || height < 1
    || width > 16384 || height > 16384 || width * height > 16000000) {
    throw new Error('Mermaid geometry exceeds 16384 px per side or 16 million pixels');
}
svg.setAttribute('viewBox', `${x} ${y} ${width} ${height}`);
svg.setAttribute('width', String(width)); svg.setAttribute('height', String(height));
svg.style.maxWidth = 'none';
return { width, height, svg: svg.outerHTML };
```

## Print one diagram

A context is closed even when parsing, SVG validation or PDF printing fails.
The parent deadline still owns a hung context close. The page's font wait concerns
installed system fonts only; CSP forbids font downloads. PDF metadata timestamps
are normalized without changing byte lengths, preserving cross-reference offsets.

```js : <<Mermaid vector rendering>>=
export async function renderVector(browser, source, theme, fontSize, bundle) {
    const context = await browser.createBrowserContext();
    try {
        const page = await context.newPage();
        await page.setViewport({ width: 1200, height: 900, deviceScaleFactor: 1 });
        const violations = await isolatePage(page);
        await page.addScriptTag({ content: bundle });
        const seed = hash(JSON.stringify([source, theme, fontSize]));
        <<Mermaid page rendering>>
        <<Mermaid PDF printing>>
    } finally { await context.close(); }
}
```

Source is passed as structured protocol data, never interpolated into HTML or
JavaScript. Mermaid's returned markup is trusted only after the policy checks;
HTML labels are disabled. After the trusted bundle loads, a second CSP disables
all further script and event-handler execution. Frames and resource attempts are checked again after
PDF printing, since print layout can otherwise trigger a delayed request.

```js : <<Mermaid page rendering>>=
await page.evaluate(async (source, config, id) => {
    const policy = document.createElement('meta');
    policy.httpEquiv = 'Content-Security-Policy'; policy.content = "script-src 'none'";
    document.head.append(policy);
    await globalThis.publicationMermaidReady;
    globalThis.mermaid.initialize(config);
    await globalThis.mermaid.parse(source);
    const result = await globalThis.mermaid.render(id, source);
    if (!result.svg.trim()) { throw new Error('Mermaid returned empty SVG: ' + JSON.stringify(result)); }

    document.body.style.backgroundColor = config.themeVariables.background;
    document.body.innerHTML = result.svg;
    const svg = document.body.querySelector('svg');
    if (svg) { svg.style.backgroundColor = config.themeVariables.background; }
    await document.fonts.ready;
}, source, configuration(theme, fontSize, seed), 'diagram-' + seed);
const geometry = await page.evaluate(measureSvg);
if (Buffer.byteLength(geometry.svg) > diagramLimits.svg) { throw new Error('Mermaid SVG exceeds 4 MiB'); }
```

The PDF remains a vector asset. The browser is not permitted to return a partial
page range for an oversized diagram: geometry is bounded, and the page is sized
to the complete SVG. A small rounding allowance prevents a trailing blank page.

```js : <<Mermaid PDF printing>>=
const bytes = await page.pdf({ width: `${geometry.width + 1}px`, height: `${geometry.height + 1}px`,
    margin: { top: 0, bottom: 0, left: 0, right: 0 }, printBackground: true,
    preferCSSPageSize: false, timeout: 15000 });
const blocked = await page.evaluate(() => globalThis.publicationViolations);
if (violations.length || blocked.length) { throw new Error('Mermaid attempted a blocked resource or navigation: ' + [...violations, ...blocked].join(', ')); }
if (bytes.length > diagramLimits.pdf) { throw new Error('Mermaid PDF exceeds 16 MiB'); }
const pdf = Buffer.from(Buffer.from(bytes).toString('latin1').replace(
    /\/(CreationDate|ModDate) \(D:\d{14}[^)]*\)/g,
    match => match.replace(/D:\d{14}/, 'D:20000101000000')), 'latin1');
return { pdf, svg: Buffer.from(geometry.svg) };
```

## Browser ownership

Puppeteer is imported only in the child. Mermaid's metadata is a static JSON
import, embedded by the publication build; no installed package lookup occurs.
The build validates the matching browser dependency pins before writing outputs.
The browser sandbox remains enabled; there is no fallback to `--no-sandbox`.
The private profile, disabled background
services and failed DNS resolution complement page-level request blocking.
JavaScript heaps are capped, but this is not a hard operating-system RSS quota.

```js : <<Mermaid browser batch>>=
export async function browserBatch(directory, executable, launch) {
    const request = JSON.parse(await fs.readFile(path.join(directory, 'request.json'), 'utf8'));
    const size = publicationFontSizeBounds.diagram;
    if (!getTheme(request.theme) || !Array.isArray(request.sources)
        || request.sources.length > diagramLimits.count || typeof request.fontSize !== 'number'
        || !Number.isFinite(request.fontSize) || request.fontSize < size.minimum
        || request.fontSize > size.maximum) {
        throw new Error('Invalid Mermaid worker request');
    }
    request.sources.forEach(validateDiagram);
    if (mermaidPackage.version !== '12.0.0') {
        throw new Error('Publication requires the pinned Mermaid 12.0.0 bundle');
    }
    const bundle = await fs.readFile(path.join(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)),
            'publication-mermaid-browser.js'), 'utf8');
    const browser = await launch({ executablePath: executable, headless: true,
        userDataDir: path.join(directory, 'profile'), timeout: 15000, protocolTimeout: 15000,
        args: ['--disable-background-networking', '--disable-component-update', '--disable-sync',
            '--no-first-run', '--host-resolver-rules=MAP * ~NOTFOUND',
            '--js-flags=--max-old-space-size=256', '--renderer-process-limit=1'] });
    <<Mermaid batch artifacts>>
}
```

Each result is complete before either artifact is written. These are private
scratch files, not publication outputs. An indexed diagnostic maps back to the
source location held by the controller; aggregate limits bound retained bytes.

```js : <<Mermaid batch artifacts>>=
try {
    let total = 0;
    for (const [index, source] of request.sources.entries()) {
        try {
            const result = await renderVector(browser, source, request.theme, request.fontSize, bundle);
            total += result.pdf.length + result.svg.length;
            if (total > diagramLimits.total) { throw new Error('Mermaid artifacts exceed 32 MiB'); }
            await fs.writeFile(path.join(directory, `${index}.pdf`), result.pdf);
            await fs.writeFile(path.join(directory, `${index}.svg`), result.svg);
        } catch (error) { throw new Error(`Diagram ${index + 1}: ${String(error)}`); }
    }
} finally { await browser.close(); }
```

Puppeteer's normal launcher detaches Chromium into a separate process group.
Instead, this worker spawns Chromium without detaching, using Puppeteer's fixed
default arguments, and connects over a loopback-only debugging endpoint. Thus
the controller's process-group kill also covers launch failures and hung closes.
The endpoint is never available to diagram page content, whose connections are
blocked by CSP and request interception; other local processes under the same user
remain outside this isolation model.

```js : <<Mermaid owned browser process>>=
export async function connectOwnedBrowser(puppeteer, options) {
    const args = await puppeteer.defaultArgs({ ...options, args: [...options.args,
        '--remote-debugging-port=0', '--remote-debugging-address=127.0.0.1'] });
    if (!Array.isArray(args) || !args.includes(`--user-data-dir=${options.userDataDir}`)) {
        throw new Error('Puppeteer did not provide the isolated browser arguments');
    }
    const home = path.dirname(options.userDataDir);
    const child = spawn(options.executablePath, args, { detached: false,
        env: { ...process.env, HOME: home, XDG_CONFIG_HOME: path.join(home, 'config'),
            XDG_CACHE_HOME: path.join(home, 'cache'), XDG_DATA_HOME: path.join(home, 'data'),
            CHROMIUM_USER_FLAGS: ' ' }, stdio: ['ignore', 'ignore', 'pipe'] });
    try {
        const endpoint = await browserEndpoint(child);
        return await puppeteer.connect({ browserWSEndpoint: endpoint, protocolTimeout: 15000 });
    } catch (error) { child.kill('SIGKILL'); throw error; }
}
```

The endpoint announcement has its own deadline and bounded stderr accumulator.
Only a loopback WebSocket endpoint is accepted. The stderr listener remains after
connection to drain the pipe, but retains no additional browser log data.

```js : <<Mermaid owned browser process>>=+
function browserEndpoint(child) {
    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
        let log = '', done = false;
        const finish = (error, endpoint) => {
            if (done) { return; }
            done = true; clearTimeout(timer);
            if (error) { reject(error); } else { resolve(endpoint); }
        };
        const timer = setTimeout(() => finish(new Error(`Chromium launch deadline exceeded: ${log}`)), 15000);
        child.once('error', error => finish(error));
        child.once('exit', code => finish(new Error(`Chromium exited ${code}: ${log}`)));
        child.stderr.on('data', bytes => {
            if (done) { return; }
            log += bytes.toString('utf8');
            if (log.length > 32768) { finish(new Error('Chromium launch log exceeds 32 KiB')); return; }
            const match = /DevTools listening on (ws:\/\/127\.0\.0\.1:\d+\/devtools\/browser\/[\w-]+)/.exec(log);
            if (match) { finish(undefined, match[1]); }
        });
    });
}
```

Browser launch failures stay actionable without asking installed-extension users
to install development dependencies. The worker never chooses a browser or
retries with weakened security. A bounded message is sufficient because the
parent retains the publication's source context.

```js : <<Mermaid worker entry>>=
async function main() {
    try {
        const { default: puppeteer } = await import('./publication-puppeteer.mjs');
        await browserBatch(process.argv[2], process.argv[3], options => connectOwnedBrowser(puppeteer, options));
    } catch (error) {
        process.stderr.write(('Mermaid browser failed (use external Node >=22.12 and a sandbox-capable system Chromium): '
            + String(error)).slice(0, 16000) + '\n', () => process.exit(1));
    }
}
if (process.argv[1] === fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)) { void main(); }
```
